        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/AsyncFunction/AsyncFunction\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">AsyncFunction()</code></a>, <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/GeneratorFunction/GeneratorFunction\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">GeneratorFunction()</code></a>, and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/AsyncGeneratorFunction/AsyncGeneratorFunction\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">AsyncGeneratorFunction()</code></a> contructors can execute their arguments as JavaScript. These are subclassed from <code class=\"notranslate\">Function()</code> so share its TT behaviour.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This duplicates the TT entry from Function (I have tested that they work in Firefox only). NOTE, the spec URL used for Function was wrong. I can't find a better one though, so I have them all linked to <a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/#trustedscript\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/trusted-types/dist/spec/#trustedscript</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">mdn/content#41507</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28778",
            "title": "TT: AsyncFunction, AsyncGeneratorFunction, GeneratorFunction",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-09T00:46:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-09T00:45:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy: gamepad</code> appears to have been removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2364557768\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23470\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470\">#23470</a> for the reasons given in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2364557768\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23470\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470/hovercard?comment_id=2423659290&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23470#issuecomment-2423659290\">#23470 (comment)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The data is definitely wierd and needs to be looked at again.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically,</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>That issues says the permission was added in 62, but in my PR of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"952418181\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/11770\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/11770/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/11770\">#11770</a> it went in at 86 behind a preference.</li>\n<li>The comment is that the feature was only supported \"on the allow iframe attribute\" based on a note that applied only to FF, so would not affect Chrome.</li>\n<li>Chrome indicate it was shipped in 103 but I can't find confirmation <a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3566388\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3566388</a></li>\n<li>Safari asserts to have supported this in tech preview 186 <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/14916/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-186/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/14916/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-186/</a> but I can't see it in <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/14205/news-from-wwdc23-webkit-features-in-safari-17-beta/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/14205/news-from-wwdc23-webkit-features-in-safari-17-beta/</a></li>\n<li>Not supported in FF, because FF only supports Feature-Policy</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/marcoscaceres/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/marcoscaceres\">@marcoscaceres</a> Do you know if this actually did release in Chrome/Safari, and if so, in what versions</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This falls out of the post <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3763982649\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42544\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42544/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42544\">mdn/content#42544</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28744",
            "title": "Permissions-Policy: gamepad - probably experimental",
